      "text": "First, we need to identify the sequence and then calculate the sum of the sequence. The sequence given is \\(1, 7, 13, 19, \\ldots, 253, 259\\). This is an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\).\n\nThe \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence can be found using the formula:\n\\[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \\]\nWe need to find the number of terms \\(n\\) in the sequence. The last term \\(a_n = 259\\). Setting up the equation:\n\\[ 259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6 \\]\n\\[ 259 = 1 + 6n - 6 \\]\n\\[ 259 = 6n - 5 \\]\n\\[ 264 = 6n \\]\n\\[ n = 44 \\]\nSo, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[ S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l) \\]\nwhere \\(l\\) is the last term. Substituting the known values:\n\\[ S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) \\]\n\\[ S_{44} = 22 \\cdot 260 \\]\n\\[ S_{44} = 5720 \\]\nWe need to find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6. We can do this by finding the remainder of 5720 divided by 6:\n\\[ 5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nSo, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is 2. Therefore, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
