      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to determine the sum of the arithmetic series given and then find the remainder when this sum is divided by 6.\n\nThe given series is \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\). This is an arithmetic series where the first term \\(a\\) is 1, the common difference \\(d\\) is 6, and the last term \\(l\\) is 259.\n\nFirst, we need to find the number of terms \\(n\\) in this series. The \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic series is given by:\n\\[a_n = a + (n-1)d\\]\nSetting \\(a_n = 259\\), we get:\n\\[259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6\\]\n\\[259 = 1 + 6n - 6\\]\n\\[259 = 6n - 5\\]\n\\[264 = 6n\\]\n\\[n = 44\\]\nSo, there are 44 terms in the series.\n\nNext, we find the sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic series:\n\\[S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l)\\]\nSubstituting the values, we get:\n\\[S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) = 22 \\cdot 260 = 5720\\]\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6. We do this by finding the remainder of 5720 when divided by 6:\n\\[5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2\\]\nSo, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is 2.\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
