      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6, we start by identifying the nature of the sequence.\n\nThe sequence given is an arithmetic progression where the first term \\(a = 1\\) and the common difference \\(d = 6\\). The general form of the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[ a_n = a + (n-1)d \\]\nSetting \\(a_n = 259\\), we can find \\(n\\) as follows:\n\\[ 259 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6 \\]\n\\[ 259 = 1 + 6n - 6 \\]\n\\[ 259 = 6n - 5 \\]\n\\[ 264 = 6n \\]\n\\[ n = 44 \\]\nSo, there are 44 terms in the sequence.\n\nThe sum \\(S_n\\) of the first \\(n\\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n\\[ S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a + l) \\]\nwhere \\(l\\) is the last term. Here, \\(n = 44\\), \\(a = 1\\), and \\(l = 259\\). Thus, the sum is:\n\\[ S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259) \\]\n\\[ S_{44} = 22 \\cdot 260 \\]\n\\[ S_{44} = 5720 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6. We do this by finding the remainder of 5720 when divided by 6:\n\\[ 5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\nSo, the remainder when 5720 is divided by 6 is 2. Therefore, the remainder when the sum \\(1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259\\) is divided by 6 is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
